                  <provenance type="#b" cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_4">Canterbury, Kent.
                        Benedictine cathedral priory of Holy Trinity or Christ
                        Church</orgName><p>Binding leaves are from the mortuary roll of John
                        Wodensburgh, prior of Christ Church; cf. Manchester, Lancs. Indep. Coll.
                        MS.</p><p> Annotations by <persName role="ann">Archbishop Parker</persName>
                        (?), e.g. f. 67v. The chronicle was annotated in s. xvi by someone with a
                        special interest in the church of Westminster. Ref. on f. 93 is probably to
                        CCCC 339.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_219">Fountains,
                        Yorkshire, Cistercian abbey of St Mary the Virgin</orgName>
                     <p>This attribution was rejected in the second edition of Medieval Libraries of
                        Great Britain (1964), which did not change in the Supplement (1987). The
                        corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card records only
                        the house name and the shelfmark, providing no further context for the
                        rejection.</p></provenance>
